Zadie Ward: Thank you.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Essentially. Um, and what that is going to be is, you know, for anybody who maybe, you know, similarly to, like, the form that you have on your website right now, right, where they're, like, downloading your pricing and information, this could, you know, replace that.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, essentially. And actually, I think I popped into the…

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.000
Zadie Ward: Yep.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Is this the right one? Yes, it is. Okay. what happens? Right? People are filling out that form. That is then what's going to trigger this workflow. So.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:22:02.000
Whitney Hodges: The way that we have it set up is that as soon as somebody fills out that form, it can, if you'd like for it to send an internal notification to you or to your husband, somebody else on your team, whoever you'd like to receive it, right, that says, you know, congrats, you've just received a new inquiry.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:19.000
Whitney Hodges: And then automatically, that's when the system's going to send out that inquiry email that I had kind of showed you within the conversations. The system also then checks for SMS compliance, meaning if they have agreed to receive those automated.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:38.000
Whitney Hodges: text messages. Um, it would just be a checkbox that they would check on your form, essentially. And if they've agreed to that, then we'd like for just a few minutes later for that automated text message to go out to them. And then it's also set up to where the course of over the next, like.

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:25.000
